+# Incidents brief, August–September 2026
+
+Follow-up status as of the 30 September meeting.
+
+## 11 August: ingest stall and full database disk
+
+**Impact:** Ingestion stalled about two and a half hours overnight; customers saw stale dashboards. No data was lost.
+**Root cause:** A malformed batch jammed ingest, which retried it endlessly; retry logs filled the database disk, which then refused writes.
+**Fix:** Restarted ingest with the bad batch set aside, then reclaimed database space and archived old logs.
+
+- Disk alert at 80% full: Sunil, done
+- Stop bad batches jamming ingest: Jonas, open (in review)
+- Paging review (no owner named): done; unanswered pages now escalate after 15 minutes
+
+## 21 September: expired API certificate
+
+**Impact:** Public API unreachable for 47 minutes (08:05–08:52) for browsers and nearly all customer integrations.
+**Root cause:** The certificate expired; its automatic renewal had failed silently since early September, using an outdated credential.
+**Fix:** Renewed the certificate and restarted the API; the renewal job is repaired and now alerts on failure.
+
+- Reminder 14 days before each expiry: Priya, done
+- Days-left expiry alert: Priya, open
+- Expiry check in weekly checklist: Tomasz, open
+- Responders write down their steps during incidents: Mara, done
